  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "V:C2(R^d), pi normalized exp(-V); source unnormalized V_eta=-log((exp(-V))*N(0,eta I)); g_eta=grad V_eta. Actual prox p_y=argmin[V(x)+||x-y||^2/(2eta)]. True unreflected R_eta,y proportional exp(-V(x)-||x-y||^2/(2eta)); gamma=N(0,I); ghat(y;G)=grad V(p_y+sqrt(eta)G).",
    "domains": "Finite Euclidean R^d with its ordinary Lebesgue and standard Gaussian probability. Source d is dimension. Finite-Hilbert/Borel or zero-dimensional representations would be explicit future extensions, not an imported source binder.",
    "quantifiers": "One fixed source potential V and eta>0; every y,yprime,u in R^d and every noise G,Gprime in R^d for deterministic (4.4)/(4.5); expectations in decomposition/MGF over G~gamma. b(y)=E_gamma[ghat(y;G)]-g_eta(y); xi(y;G)=ghat(y;G)-E_gamma[ghat(y;G)] so E_gamma xi=0. No supplied bias/stochastic-error certificate.",
    "assumptions": "Source standing V C2, 0<alpha<=beta, alpha I<=Hess V<=beta I everywhere; normalized beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, kappa>=1. Positive smoothing eta. Lemma4.2 does not itself print eta<=1; adjacent Lemma4.1 explicitly does. No reference-point, initial-law, oracle-runtime, supplied partition/moments/coupling/MGF/prox selector premises are part of Lemma4.2.",
    "conclusions": "||b_eta(y)||<=eta^(3/2)*sqrt(d); E_gamma exp(<u,xi_eta(y;G)>)<=exp(eta*||u||^2/2); ||ghat(y;G)-ghat(yprime;G)||<=||y-yprime||; ||ghat(y;G)-ghat(y;Gprime)||<=sqrt(eta)||G-Gprime||. Full centered Gaussian directional MGF, not just variance/subexponential/tail with an unspecified universal constant.",
    "scope": "Actual Gaussian gradient evaluator law is (ghat(y;·))#gamma; its argument law N(p_y,eta I) is generally different from true R_eta,y. Standardized r_y is affine pushforward of R_eta,y and has normalized density exp(-Q_y), Q_y=||u||^2/2+rho_y. PBPS reflected laws/quarter scales, HMC phase kernels, main sampling guarantees and cost are separate.",
    "constants": "Bias coefficient1, MGF exponent eta||u||^2/2, common-noise input Lip1, noise Lip sqrt(eta). First(4.6) W2(r_y,gamma)<=sqrt(I(r_y|gamma)), then <=eta sqrt(E_r||U||^2)<=eta sqrt(d). Gaussian T2 coefficient2 and Gaussian entropy-Fisher coefficient1/2 cancel exactly."
  },
  "normalization": {
    "base": "Z_V=int exp(-V)dx finite positive is an internally required consequence of positive lower curvature, not a new source assumption; pi=exp(-V)/Z_V.",
    "smoothing": "exp(-V_eta(y))=(2*pi*eta)^(-d/2)*int exp(-V(x)-||x-y||^2/(2eta))dx. Negative log normalized smoothed density U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V; gradients agree; never silently substitute these potentials as equal.",
    "posterior": "R_eta,y has its own actual finite positive normalizer. Standardizing u=(x-p_y)/sqrt(eta) gives Q_y and Jacobian eta^(d/2); constant-shift and Jacobian cancel only after actual partitions are established.",
    "rho": "rho_y(u)=V(p_y+sqrt(eta)u)-V(p_y)-sqrt(eta)<grad V(p_y),u>; rho_y(0)=0, grad rho_y(0)=0, 0<=Hess rho_y<=eta I; Q Hessian lies I..(1+eta)I.",
    "score_identity": "g_eta(y)=int grad V dR_eta,y=grad V(p_y)+eta^(-1/2)E_r grad rho_y; ghat=grad V(p_y)+eta^(-1/2)grad rho_y(G). Source3.1/4.1 differentiation/IBP requires genuine domination/integrability, not an arbitrary conditional representative."
  },
  "range_audit": {
    "literal": "S3.SS1.p1.1 eta>0; S4.Thmtheorem2 has no printed eta<=1 premise. S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1 alone says 0<eta<=1. Source Lemma4.2 proof chain as printed does not consume eta<=1.",
    "future_scoped_choice": "A future statement with 0<eta<=1 should be explicitly called a restricted analytic slice if claiming literal full Lemma4.2 equivalence; do not insert the neighboring lemma cap silently. No future signature has been approved here.",
    "numerical": "S2.p2.2 only actual proximal oracle use/implementation is restricted to a<=1/(2beta). This is distinct from analytic eta>0 or eta<=1 and does not establish query count/work for analytic full-range evaluator."
  },
  "gaussian_background": [
    {
      "name": "Talagrand standard Gaussian quadratic transport-entropy inequality (T2)",
      "primary_citation": "S4.SS1.p4.3 names Talagrand; no direct bibliography link/theorem number in this paragraph",
      "formula": "W2(nu,gamma)^2<=2 KL(nu|gamma)",
      "contract": "Actual probability nu, gamma=N(0,I); extended entropy convention for lack of absolute continuity; actual finite second moments/finite entropy needed for finite useful consumer. Here nu=r_y must be produced, not supplied as a transport certificate.",
      "role": "First half of source first4.6."
    },
    {
      "name": "Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality",
      "primary_citation": "S4.SS1.p4.3 names Gaussian LSI without direct numbered reference",
      "formula": "Ent_gamma(h^2)<=2 int ||grad h||^2 dgamma; for density f=dnu/dgamma with actual sqrt(f) Sobolev regularity: KL(nu|gamma)<=0.5 int ||grad log f||^2 dnu",
      "contract": "gamma probability; h real Sobolev/finite energy with actual approximation/entropy extension; normalized nu and actual nonnegative RN density, not a supplied KL/Fisher bound. For r_y: f=(Z_gamma/Z_Q)exp(-rho_y), grad log f=-grad rho_y, Fisher finite from genuine position L2 and rho Lip. Finite entropy follows quadratic rho growth; all constants/normalizers genuine.",
      "role": "Together with T2 produces W2<=sqrt(Fisher). Source leaves analytic details/background proof omitted."
    },
    {
      "name": "Standard Gaussian Lipschitz concentration / centered Laplace transform",
      "primary_citation": "S4.SS1.p5.2 names standard Gaussian concentration; no bib/theorem-number link there",
      "formula": "For actual real L-Lipschitz h, all t in R: E_gamma exp(t(h-E_gamma h))<=exp(t^2 L^2/2)",
      "contract": "Measurable real scalar Lipschitz h and its genuine finite Gaussian expectation; actual exponential integrability derived, not assumed as a conclusion certificate. The exact Laplace form must be proved or faithfully sourced; a tail bound alone is not the exact coefficient1/2 MGF contract. A Gaussian LSI/Herbst route is an authored background completion, not a route printed in p5.2.",
      "consumer": "h(G)=<u,ghat(y;G)> has L=sqrt(eta)||u||; apply t=1 (or all t) after actual centering to obtain4.3."
    },
    {
      "name": "IBP position moment, not Gaussian functional concentration",
      "primary_citation": "S4.SS1.p4.3 final clause",
      "formula": "E_r <U,grad Q(U)>=d; Q strongly convex1 and grad Q(0)=0 imply E_r||U||^2<=d",
      "contract": "Actual normalized r, genuine position/derivative products integrable and valid full-space integration by parts. No assumed position bound or arbitrary strongly convex moment certificate.",
      "role": "Last4.6 and genuine finite Fisher prerequisite; packet27 historical review is not this source contract proof."
    }
